<title>GERMANY: Duesseldorf air cargo rises 24.8pct in March.</title>
<headline>Duesseldorf air cargo rises 24.8pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total flown air cargo handled at Duesseldorf airport (DUS) continued its strong 1997 growth with a 24.8 percent rise in March, figures from the German airports association ADV show.</p>
<p>In the first quarter of 1997, air cargo handled at the airport rose 21.8 percent on the same period last year to 16,662 tonnes, the monthly ADV traffic report said.</p>
<p>The following tables show cargo handled at Duesseldorf airport in March and for January-March in tonnes, with year-on-year percentage changes.</p>
<p>    March 1997		Monthly total	Pct change</p>
<p>Total flown cargo		6,226		Up 24.8</p>
<p>Exports			    2,899		Up 27.4</p>
<p>Imports			    3,185		Up 25.1</p>
<p>Transit				142		N/A</p>
<p>    Jan-Mar 1997	    Cumulative total    Pct change</p>
<p>Total flown cargo	     16,662		Up 21.8</p>
<p>Exports			    7,493		Up 23.5</p>
<p>Imports			    8,757		Up 21.6</p>
<p>Transit				412		N/A</p>
<p>Source: German Airports Association ADV, market research department.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
